[{"id":"VRCE-4-62-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":1,"english":"Having praised me with these and many other words, and bidden me adieu that one skilled in speech, entered his own habitation.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.92,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b29b6a9dd98feee61a881ede1309b1692997b7b04f6f56b7ca727c16755557ed","compact":"8f568e986330e39a0d4968d33974f191b46ee4d97cd1e3580705fa7c32e29a2d","nasal":"8f568e986330e39a0d4968d33974f191b46ee4d97cd1e3580705fa7c32e29a2d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":2,"english":"Issuing out gently from the cave of that mountain, I, ascending Vindhya, was expecting you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"414444825ed6eb41469f192d08ccbcaaaf234703440f2e12c13d3141feb61323","compact":"233cdd3f7d3c5a8461e83cdcbee2c1ac92be60840fc46e126c34a9f797af6b35","nasal":"c373a5935250cca349b809339f6b72aa2804eb0cf81bdd0be76859b56b5b5e32"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":3,"english":"The space covered by the time intervening between then and to-day is a little over an hundred years;* and laying up in my heart the speech of that ascetic I have been awaiting season and place. *The commentator says the period is one hundred and eight years.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0515de654698468090f3269cce8daa4398828efc144c12c1f23c6a3ad396f7e3","compact":"de9f821fb8879ddf0f8d87f04353c1f5d1d215e302ec686cc78ec567cf92173d","nasal":"de9f821fb8879ddf0f8d87f04353c1f5d1d215e302ec686cc78ec567cf92173d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":4,"english":"Setting out on his great journey, on Niśākara having gone to heaven, I distracted with various thoughts, have been consumed by grief. For the loss of my plumage.-","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.848,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4c9f7923e15ccce03f7476c6f0c348e1f09d27677a28c82ba3390690f16b0099","compact":"ed4c2e419c4f2f0ebc207e9886a3c5d8006c7ca3c9e0eb556e58e7e157c08b1c","nasal":"ed4c2e419c4f2f0ebc207e9886a3c5d8006c7ca3c9e0eb556e58e7e157c08b1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":5,"english":"My rising intention of doing away with myself I have suppressed in consideration of the words of the ascetic. The reason which he had imparted to me for preserving my life, has removed my pains even as a flaming fire (dispels darkness).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.782,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76d3072f57c3cff01d482570b9c0e801d1e6fd02386fccb151b8d26ee63f1883","compact":"00254049ae557524b97e66ea56d601a1674c7e8715b7a3d4c2f45128ac53dc99","nasal":"00254049ae557524b97e66ea56d601a1674c7e8715b7a3d4c2f45128ac53dc99"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":6,"english":"And knowing the prowess of the impious Rāvana, I said in rage to my son, versed in speech,-'Hearing her lamentation, and knowing them bereft of Sītā, why didst you not deliver her?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c385b75f3f7b5e92921a2bd461dd4354ac9ad1f3c9e2c3763475f5380bc0eb28","compact":"62b71d39a27119081904144530fad4781dba1ead2845b73da40157c4d8b324e8","nasal":"62b71d39a27119081904144530fad4781dba1ead2845b73da40157c4d8b324e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":7,"english":"My son did not do this good office to Daſaratha, influenced by affection for him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e30dcb3e402fc3749535b204421838edb125a3ce5888cfff6ca9bab0151f90c","compact":"d6cdc2ff91317715e8bf8f30e366bd34d42575e90fbac9c51991cadbb84acc77","nasal":"d6cdc2ff91317715e8bf8f30e366bd34d42575e90fbac9c51991cadbb84acc77"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":8,"english":"As he was speaking thus in the midst of the monkeys, his wings sprang up in presence of the rangers of the forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"283b2cd42ad8f1c6914049cd3ae98a4d331f6fd311eac1bb9a257b2305428376","compact":"39c93d2c5dae3595c51660d1dd4d3bf5467d60065b9b85aa81c86a8ca2abcc26","nasal":"39c93d2c5dae3595c51660d1dd4d3bf5467d60065b9b85aa81c86a8ca2abcc26"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":9,"english":"Thereupon, seeing his person furnished with grown pinions hued like the infant sun, he experienced incomparable raptures, and addressed the monkeys, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e7efb039700504433bad6250cbf22baf882aab1f92d13e25b57b4d97c3f49ce","compact":"d8e4a23bf743d61d546a088fd17e8dacfc734f77faaf87d046fb134f81d419c1","nasal":"d8e4a23bf743d61d546a088fd17e8dacfc734f77faaf87d046fb134f81d419c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":10,"english":"By the grace of that Rājarși of immeasurable energy, my wings, which had been burnt up by the rays of the sun, have grown again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.344,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7abc9ecdd8d84604339545170ecf6ed1da86e706b034086331fe917ee66bc6f2","compact":"8cb436cd4a6e484290fd64575097346b6c84f28f815583d62776d2b2ee6c04fd","nasal":"8cb436cd4a6e484290fd64575097346b6c84f28f815583d62776d2b2ee6c04fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":11,"english":"To-day I have got back) the strength and prowess which I possessed while my youth was yet present.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64ad5240e85f3641f2acc22c38585d5660144a5b4dd13c9339c3e38b1e3a7eb8","compact":"a948d6cfd91ff176728bbc9a56a3c55dba50961f25ecd139199afc8e1411b09e","nasal":"a948d6cfd91ff176728bbc9a56a3c55dba50961f25ecd139199afc8e1411b09e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":12,"english":"Do you strive every way. You shall meet with Sītā. And my getting (back) my wings inspires (us) with confidence as to success.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c26bdd94edf1d5d9974cd559dd5932a9471c7b5d210d65cb9186b6ef9ac35ef","compact":"4f82e25c5cf58b6192a7e60dcbf57e7f67ffc16875a01108c7c5b7587e0f42fa","nasal":"4f82e25c5cf58b6192a7e60dcbf57e7f67ffc16875a01108c7c5b7587e0f42fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":13,"english":"Having said this to all the monkeys, that ranger of the sky and best of birds. Sampāti, anxious to ascertain his power of flight, flew up from the mountain summits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.616,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e0c87715e8fa234093845a7b8c659e9381fcd1ffd456099ac18fdd774015c856","compact":"fe132b0adfc3cf0421a8fff5e57268fd7585caacb8479192d79a9421e8442420","nasal":"5e3f01f12d7829361edc21397b613cae358ffb7a39751fabf1ee2e68d7f58bde"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing his words, those powerful monkeys, with vigour (enhanced, seeing success before them, felt the height of joy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e3773705387c3771bed143173497cea7b46abfa2e2e43dbf696e09f228b604dd","compact":"01eabcaf8048894222374f664e8ef7c77c162d61579dc3cac6ed8ccab7453f36","nasal":"01eabcaf8048894222374f664e8ef7c77c162d61579dc3cac6ed8ccab7453f36"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-62-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":62,"verse":15,"english":"Then those foremost of monkeys, in vigour resembling the Wind, getting occasion for displaying their prowess, intent upon searching the Janaka's daughter, set forward towards the quarter crested by Abhijit.* * Abhijitabhimukhan (acc.) Abhijit—the name of a star. Abhijit may also mean-he who is to be conquered. Then the sense would be the region in which Rāvana was.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-63-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4062015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d9a49c55ef0c9c3364703d619a39aac8c8b079f0c8d59de247730c3255d1aaf","compact":"a3f595d81296e75150fa53986447ecaedfb4e16e9f3b33fa1f7debd8c8090595","nasal":"a3f595d81296e75150fa53986447ecaedfb4e16e9f3b33fa1f7debd8c8090595"}}]
